WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.988
Step 5 collects the second week,
and this is the step to watch.

2
00:00:03.988 --> 00:00:06.324
Oracle rescheduled the maintenance.

3
00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:10.675
In Oracle's model, that arrives as a
new announcement in the same chain.

4
00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:15.015
The kit keeps the chain's latest,
so the database maintenance now

5
00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:19.437
starts November 29 instead of
November 22, with its new window end.

6
00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:22.081
And it's still one
notice, with the same ID,

7
00:00:22.081 --> 00:00:26.725
so Chapter 6 updates the existing
task instead of opening a second one.

8
00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:28.962
Read every announcement on its own,

9
00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.180
and the old window would
linger next to the new one.
